// name Finnegans Wake
// id index
// +frag.id.show -
// brief James Joyce, Finnegans Wake: the text, page by page and line by line.
// C A control card: spaced, justified paragraphs; the headwords of list items in bold.
// +html.style p { margin: 0.6em 0; text-align: justify; }
// +bd ^(– )?(?P<open>)(?:(?!\. )[^:]){1,40}?(?P<close>)(?=: )
// +bd ^(?P<open>)(\d{4}|[A-Z])(?P<close>)(?=\. )
James Joyce, _Finnegans Wake_. This deck is the text of the book, one card per
printed page, one fragment per printed line, made to be read slowly and
annotated. Each line shows its identifier, the page and the line number
(p003-04 is the line 3.04); this is how notes and links refer to it.
/ id top

; head
/ level 3
/ id pages
Pages

> – Contents: every page, by book and chapter.
/ += . "Contents" -> !contents

> – The whole book, page after page: series book (or all at once, flat).
/ += . "series book" -> series_book_compact.html
/ += . "flat" -> series_book_flat.html

> – Book I: I.1, I.2, I.3, I.4, I.5, I.6, I.7, I.8.
/ += . "Book I(?=:)" -> series_I_compact.html
/ += . "I\.1" -> series_I.1_compact.html
/ += . "I\.2" -> series_I.2_compact.html
/ += . "I\.3" -> series_I.3_compact.html
/ += . "I\.4" -> series_I.4_compact.html
/ += . "I\.5" -> series_I.5_compact.html
/ += . "I\.6" -> series_I.6_compact.html
/ += . "I\.7" -> series_I.7_compact.html
/ += . "I\.8" -> series_I.8_compact.html

> – Book II: II.1, II.2, II.3, II.4.
/ += . "Book II(?=:)" -> series_II_compact.html
/ += . "II\.1" -> series_II.1_compact.html
/ += . "II\.2" -> series_II.2_compact.html
/ += . "II\.3" -> series_II.3_compact.html
/ += . "II\.4" -> series_II.4_compact.html

> – Book III: III.1, III.2, III.3, III.4.
/ += . "Book III(?=:)" -> series_III_compact.html
/ += . "III\.1" -> series_III.1_compact.html
/ += . "III\.2" -> series_III.2_compact.html
/ += . "III\.3" -> series_III.3_compact.html
/ += . "III\.4" -> series_III.4_compact.html

> – Book IV.
/ += . "Book IV" -> series_IV_compact.html

> – The first page: 3.
/ += . "3\." -> !p003

; head
/ level 3
/ id about
About the text

> – Editions: the printings and transcriptions used, how the text was
  established, and the form of the apparatus of variants (the footnotes that
  record where the first edition, 1939, and the corrected Viking
  printing, 1958, differ).
/ += . "Editions" -> !editions

> – Tools: the programs that establish the text and generate the deck.
/ += . "Tools" -> !tools

> – Glosses: the notes "ט word" in the right margin link to the glosses
  of finwake.com, a glossary of Finnegans Wake, where the word is explained.
/ += . "finwake\.com" -> https://finwake.com/

> – Notebooks: the notes "Ω" in the right margin link a phrase to the entry of
  Joyce's notebooks from which it comes, on the James Joyce Digital Archive
  (click the phrase there to see the entry).
/ += . "James Joyce Digital Archive" -> https://jjda.ie/f/fwhome.htm

> – Readings: a footnote "ק" on the line where a recorded reading starts links to
  the recording at that line: James Joyce's own reading of the end of I.8
  (1929), and the reading of Books I and II.1 by A Poetry Channel.

; head
/ level 3
/ id licence
